{
  "name": "Search Console index watcher",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Search Console index watcher\n\n**What it does**\nEvery morning, checks your most important URLs with the Google Search Console URL Inspection API and alerts Slack when a page that was indexed is no longer indexed.\n\n**You need**\nA verified Search Console property, a Google OAuth2 credential with the `webmasters.readonly` scope, Google Sheets and Slack credentials.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Create a Google OAuth2 API credential named `Google Search Console account` (scope in the README) and connect it on **Inspect URL in Search Console**.\n2. Set your property in **Your settings** and your sheet ID in both sheet nodes.\n3. List your URLs in the sheet, run once to record today's state, then activate.\n\nBuilt by AI Strike Force, aistrikeforce.com",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 500
      },
      "id": "0a71af18-50ad-476e-ab48-fe1df691a2c5",
      "name": "Search Console index watcher",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Edit me\nYour Search Console property exactly as Google shows it:\n`sc-domain:example.com` for a domain property, or `https://www.example.com/` (with the trailing slash) for a URL prefix property.",
        "height": 270,
        "width": 210,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "edbb6365-b6e7-4cb8-a2d4-6059585f42a8",
      "name": "Edit me: property",
